  <!-- SECTION 2: LIVE BINARY MUTATOR -->
  <div class="cs-panel active cs-panel-divider" id="cs-panel-mutate">
    <div class="cs-panel-header cs-panel-header-stack">
      <div class="cs-header-top">
        <strong class="cs-panel-title">2. Pain Point: Updating 1 String or Array in Binary Formats (Arrow / FlatBuffers) Forces a Full Buffer Rebuild</strong>
        <p class="cs-sub">
          Immutable columnar/binary buffers (Apache Arrow, FlatBuffers) cannot mutate variable-length strings or arrays without unpacking and rebuilding the entire table. <code>capnstruct</code> stores fixed-size fields in an 8-byte-aligned <code>#[repr(C)]</code> table and variable-length strings/slices in a relative-offset <strong>tail arena</strong> so you can mutate fields directly on the binary view:
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-how-grid">
        <div class="cs-how-card">
          <strong>1. Shorter / Equal Edit (<code>0 Allocs</code>)</strong>
          <span>Overwrites UTF-8 bytes or slice elements directly inside the existing slot; records reclaimed bytes in <code>.compactionRatio</code>.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-how-card">
          <strong>2. Longer Edit (<code>Tail Append</code>)</strong>
          <span>Extends in place if at the tail tip (<code>0 dead bytes</code>), or bump-allocates at the tail end and updates the 8-byte <code>[u32 relOff, u32 len]</code> pointer.</span>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-how-card">
          <strong>3. <code>.compact()</code> (<code>Wire Ready</code>)</strong>
          <span>Strips dead tail bytes in a single pass and rebinds the view in-place before sending over WebSocket / RPC.</span>
        </div>
      </div>
        <pre class="cs-qs-code" id="cs-mutator-code"><code><span class="cs-kw">const</span> User  = <span class="cs-fn">struct</span>(<span class="cs-str">'User'</span>, &#123; id: u32, name: str, scores: <span class="cs-fn">slice</span>(u32) &#125;); <span class="cs-cm">// 20B #[repr(C)] stride + variable tail arena</span>
<span class="cs-kw">const</span> users = User.<span class="cs-fn">from</span>([&#123; id: 1, name: <span class="cs-str">'Ada Lovelace'</span>, scores: [10, 20, 30] &#125;, &#123; id: 2, name: <span class="cs-str">'Alan Turing'</span>, scores: [40, 50] &#125;]);
<span id="cs-mut-code-line" class="cs-live-var">users.at(0).name = 'Ada';</span> <span class="cs-cm" id="cs-mut-code-comment">// &rarr; click any button below or edit a row input to execute live on the binary buffer</span></code></pre>
        <div class="cs-actions">
