        <p class="cs-sub">
          Sharing memory between TypeScript and Rust/Go WebAssembly usually forces a choice between slow <code>serde-wasm-bindgen</code> FFI copies or brittle manual <code>DataView.getFloat64(ptr + 16, true)</code> offset math. Define your schema once in TypeScript, allocate directly inside <code>WebAssembly.Memory</code> via <code>Schema.inWasm(wasmMem, rows)</code>, and generate verified Rust <code>#[repr(C)]</code> structs with safe <code>.as_str(arena)</code>, <code>.as_slice(arena)</code>, and <code>.as_ref(arena)</code> accessors:
